// @check
// @error-at 8:26 name every parameter of a function type, or none of them
// @error-at 9:31 name every parameter of a function type, or none of them
// @error-at 10:16 a parameter name is written only in a function type `(name: T) => R`
// Parameter names in a function type are all or none (DECISIONS.md, "Parameter names in a
// function type are documentation"): a half-named list reads as though the unnamed slots
// were something else. A name inside a plain parenthesized type, which is not a function
// type, names nothing. Each refusal points at the list's closing `)`.
type Mixed = (fn: i32, i64) => i32
type Tail = (i32, rcx: i64, i64) => i32
type P = (x: i32)
